      "problem": "If $-16{log}_{7}⁡(x-128)=-48$, then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange our equation to isolate the logarithmic term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-16{log}_{7}⁡(x-128) & =-48 \\\\ {log}_{7}⁡(x-128) & =\\frac{-48}{-16} \\\\ {log}_{7}⁡(x-128) & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo remove the logarithm, we exponentiate both sides of the equation. The base of the logarithm is $7,$ so we use this base for the exponentiation as well:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{7}⁡(x-128) & =3 \\\\ {7}^{{log}_{7}⁡(x-128)} & ={7}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since exponentiation is the inverse function of the logarithm, we get ${7}^{{log}_{7}⁡(x-128)}=x-128.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-128 & ={7}^{3} \\\\ x-128 & =343 \\\\ x & =471.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
